{"path":"locale/localeconv","title":"std::localeconv","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>localeconv","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/locale/localeconv","section":"locale","kind":"page","summary":"The localeconv function obtains a pointer to a static object of type std::lconv, which represents numeric and monetary formatting rules of the current C locale.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/clocale\">&lt;clocale&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/locale/lconv\"><span class=\"kw2008\">std::<span class=\"me2\">lconv</span></span></a><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> localeconv<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>The <code>localeconv</code> function obtains a pointer to a static object of type <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/locale/lconv\">std::lconv</a></span>, which represents numeric and monetary formatting rules of the current C locale.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>Pointer to the current <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/locale/lconv\">std::lconv</a></span> object. \n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>Modifying the object references through the returned pointer is undefined behavior.\n</p><p><code>std::localeconv</code> modifies a static object, calling it from different threads without synchronization is undefined behavior.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;clocale&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/locale/setlocale\"><span class=\"kw2007\">std::<span class=\"me2\">setlocale</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/locale/LC_categories\"><span class=\"kw2009\">LC_ALL</span></a>, <span class=\"st0\">\"ja_JP.UTF-8\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/locale/lconv\"><span class=\"kw2008\">std::<span class=\"me2\">lconv</span></span></a><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> lc <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">localeconv</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Japanese currency symbol: \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> lc<span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>currency_symbol\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'('</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> lc<span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>int_curr_symbol <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\")<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>Japanese currency symbol: ￥(JPY )</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/locale/setlocale\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>setlocale</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  gets and sets the current C locale <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/locale/lconv\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>lconv</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  formatting details, returned by <span class=\"t-lc\"><strong class=\"selflink\">std::localeconv</strong></span> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/c/locale/localeconv\">C documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>localeconv</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"locale","title":"Localization library"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::localeconv","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. The localeconv function obtains a pointer to a static object of type std::lconv, which represents numeric and monetary…"},{"label":"Parameters","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Return value","note":"Pointer to the current std::lconv object."},{"label":"Notes","note":"Modifying the object references through the returned pointer is undefined behavior."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"setlocale","note":"gets and sets the current C locale"},{"label":"lconv","note":"formatting details, returned by std::localeconv"}]}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":125,"codeBlockCount":2}
